WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.760
- Why you should not go into consulting.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.270
This is the topic for today's video.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.380
It's a bit of an unusual topic if you know

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.700
the other videos on my channel,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.760
and indeed I also want to make the format

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.600
of today's video a little
bit different than otherwise

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.770
because today I really want
to give you a real talk.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.252
I want to show some real stories to you,

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.990
tell you really about
my personal experiences

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.420
and thereby talk about
why I really think that

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.290
for some people probably
consulting is not the right thing.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.180
And also really explain that to you.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.110
What really the downsides
of the career are.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.010
I hope also touch a couple of things

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.770
which are not the obvious reasons.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.950
Like you travel a lot,
I think we all know this

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.720
but let's really go into
the details of this.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.853
And so indeed the format
I want to do it here today

00:00:43.853 --> 00:00:45.540
also in the video format is that

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.460
I will just sit down here with you.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.570
I wrote a couple of notes
here on my piece of paper

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.680
and I just really want to have a

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.710
a heart to heart conversation with you,

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.560
which is really Frank, probably also

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.810
a bit less edited this video than usual

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.710
so apologize if maybe
I just talk a bit more

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.120
or are less structured
than usual, because again

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.520
this would just be due to
the nature of this video

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.190
just because I want to be as frank

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.930
and as open as possible with you today.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.780
So in this spirit welcome
to another coffee break

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.490
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.000
I will of course drink coffee

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.820
as usual. And I will probably put it down

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.860
here next to me, but please do not wonder

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.890
if I'll casually pick it up again.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.730
On my channel I want to help you

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.840
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.040
And again, just to start this also off

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.800
to make sure that I'm not
being misunderstood here.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.900
If you've seen other videos on my channel,

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.270
you know that I'm in general
a very big fan of consulting.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.590
I'm a very big proponent of consulting

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:48.160
and this was not just
fake, I truly believe that

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.940
I truly believe that consulting is a great

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.810
extraordinary career opportunity

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.500
for many many people out there,
I really mean this by heart.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.940
Though it's not only positive
what you experience there,

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.730
for sure I had some dark moments for sure

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.480
to me there happened things
which weren't that great.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.300
And I want to talk
about this as well, also

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.910
on the channel, just, just in
terms of being fair, right?

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.560
Because I believe that if you decide

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.700
yourself to start
consulting, then you should

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.660
know what you're getting yourself into.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.520
And then also what maybe some things are

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.090
which may be a bit nicer
in other career paths.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.820
Because of course, even
though I like consulting

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.590
a lot by no means I want to claim that

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.770
consulting is the only career path

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.090
that you can pursue to become successful

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.200
or to be happy or to have a great life.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.960
Of course, there are
many other alternatives.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.240
I mean, I hope that
this is obvious as well.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.940
So let's talk about these things.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.730
And I have prepared three
points I want to talk about.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.740
And maybe if we just kind of
read the topic of the point

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.530
it might sound a bit
obvious to you, but again

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.890
I hope to touch also a couple
of not so obvious points here.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.070
And the first point I want
to talk about is the pressure

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:59.440
the pressure that you will
feel when working in consulting

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.920
especially also as a junior,
really from the start.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.550
And here just really try to put yourselves

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.480
in the shoes of a young consultant.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.550
How will your day look like?

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.560
And I'm especially as always talking

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.920
about these very large tier
one strategy consulting firms

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.000
with some other firms that
might be a bit different.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.610
Of course not all firms are the
same and so on and so forth.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.520
You know this right?

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.300
But let's talk about this type of firm.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.810
And indeed they're often from day one,

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:29.940
from week one after the
first onboarding days or so

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.950
you will be sitting at the client

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.230
on an actual client project,

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.060
and you will have
significant responsibilities.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.660
The team sizes are very small on a typical

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.010
MBB type of project, It will be one of

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.470
two, three, four, five consultants.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.250
And you will very early on be

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.350
responsible for full work stream.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.450
And if for whatever
reason your work stream

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:55.200
isn't doing well the pressure is on.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.600
Let me just tell you this.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:00.000
Because everybody is so
loaded, so full of work.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.790
It's not the case as in many other

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.330
larger companies that
your colleagues can just

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.690
pick up the work, can just help you out

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.690
necessarily can just do the work for you,

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.750
for whatever reason, you
do not really manage.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.370
Of course there will be a project lead

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.120
who will coach you, who will help you,

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.550
who will really benefit you also try to

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:19.940
develop you, and in difficult
meetings, also join you.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.433
But even then very early
you will have meetings.

00:04:22.433 --> 00:04:25.370
With also rather senior
clients on many projects.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.720
Alone, you will sit alone with them.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.250
And then, again, for all kinds

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.730
of reasons that wouldn't be unusual

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:33.220
that maybe a client isn't happy with you,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.210
with your work, with the
value that you deliver

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.160
with the results that you bring.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.780
And he will criticize
you and you might not get

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.390
along well with him, or her,
or whatever the client is.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.290
The client might complain
to your project lead,

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.970
to your partner. And then
depending on how it goes,

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.040
I mean, again depends
on the circumstances,

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.320
but then rather quickly sometimes

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.840
you will really also be very quickly

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.540
in the focus of the critique.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.740
And if this happens, also just mentally,

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.770
psychologically that
can be extremely tough.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:06.500
Imagine going into the
team room every day,

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.400
you're working with clients who you know

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.120
don't like you don't appreciate you

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.160
don't want to work with you.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.230
And of course this also often
has political reasons, right?

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.190
Some clients might
literally be incentivized

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.200
to not make you succeed, to make you fail.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.890
And of course, in an ideal situation

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.300
your team will recognize
this, will help you out.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.100
will support you, And this is also

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.720
how it is most of the
times, but not always.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.010
And you know, this can really be tough.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.060
And I also made a video about that,

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.580
talking about stress and
anxiety in situations like this

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.680
I will link it somewhere above here

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.130
where I'm sharing things like this.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.870
And I also explaining a bit
more also more personal stories.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:44.010
But I mean, I can tell you,
let, let me be honest here.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:48.180
I have projects where I really
just felt like so miserable.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.830
It was psychologically so bad.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:53.530
I remember one time I just
went to the client toilet

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.300
locked myself into a toilet cabin

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.740
and just because I couldn't
handle the situation anymore

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.540
in the team room, sitting
together with the colleagues

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.770
just coming out of a client meeting

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:08.290
just really being heavily
criticized by the client.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.650
And then also often feeling powerless

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.000
because sometimes of course the criticism

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.100
is right, but especially as a junior,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.920
you will lack sometimes
also the political agility

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.830
to really play this in the right way.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.370
There are also things that
are out of your control.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.630
And very frankly, I've seen colleagues

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.330
who just were crushed by that.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.740
I mean, who really spent
like one or two years

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.520
in this atmosphere and
really psychologically

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.930
mentally, probably even had like some more

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.660
or less like lasting damages from that

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.690
because it can be like extremely
difficult, extremely tough.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:41.390
And if you do not develop some

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:44.430
some really mental resilience strategies

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.010
then this can really take a toll on you.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.320
And again now, I, also
don't take me wrong.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.600
I don't want to now make
consulting sound like

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.550
mental abuse or anything like that.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.270
I mean, clearly there are many, many

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.510
other things where you
have much worse experience

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:00.260
than what you can experience there.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:01.810
But again, a thing on some people

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.030
it can be extremely tough,
extremely difficult.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.960
I for sure had my dark moments as well.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.010
I believe there's like,
almost no consultant

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.780
for sure no consultant I personally know

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.250
who didn't have like one or two situations

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.140
on projects, but I really feel badly

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:21.590
also really mentally for
all kinds of reasons.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.030
Of course, the great
thing in consulting is

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:25.450
that then, after the project is

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:26.990
always the next project where you then

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.220
work with a new team, with a new client,

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.770
with a new situation.

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:32.390
And also here in terms of your career

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.960
only if you fail on one project,

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:36.306
for whatever reason this doesn't mean

00:07:36.306 --> 00:07:37.470
that you need to leave the firm

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.420
or that you need to get
kicked out or whatever, right?

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.170
I mean, it's not like that, but still,

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.040
this mental pressure is a thing.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.860
And also like to compare
this to some other jobs

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.630
because I mean, there
are jobs where you just

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:52.410
go into the office, you sit
down there, you do your work.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.510
And then at 5 or 6:00
PM, you leave the office.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.320
And then at home there's
really nothing else

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.752
you need to think about anymore.

00:07:58.752 --> 00:08:00.450
Like you have like an empty head.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.960
These are these more, If you
want to call it this way,

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.510
simple jobs, I don't know, don't mean this

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:07.160
in any derogatory way,
but this for sure is not

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:09.050
how your job in consulting will be.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.080
I mean, you will leave the office,

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.560
You will sit at your desk at night,

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.640
late at night still continue to work

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.170
potentially late after midnight,

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:19.300
next morning, back in the team room.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.030
And then on the Friday on the weekend.

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.876
Yes. Like there's a strong culture

00:08:22.876 --> 00:08:23.930
at least what I experienced to

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:26.290
not work on the weekend, but for sure,

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.610
you're already thinking of Monday.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.270
I mean, clearly it's not a job

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.260
that you just have an empty head

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.670
once you're home or anything like this.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:35.220
Especially if you compare
this to some other careers.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:38.730
So this is the first
truth, The first downside

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:41.500
the first thing you need to
be aware of; this pressure.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.050
And of course, many
things I just talked about

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.200
are very closely and directly related also

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.430
to the learning curve.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:49.400
I mean, these are situations just

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.730
while you learn so much, I mean,

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.740
it is just because you
are under so much pressure

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:55.640
that you develop yourself
in such a quick way

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.040
that you need to learn
this political game.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.790
You need to learn to
interacting with senior clients

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.780
that have their own agenda and so on.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.560
I mean, also again you
need to understand that

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.810
this is closely linked, right?

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:09.580
But still, this is part
of the reality as well.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:10.683
This is what it is.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.560
So hope I didn't talk
already talk too much

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.360
and too long here, I
have a bit of a feeling

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.060
this one might get into
a bit of a longer video

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.163
but let me now take a sip of coffee here.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.950
And because of the second
point, I want to talk

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.090
about the second thing
that I believe really

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:35.090
people underestimate
is this travel aspect.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.820
And I know I said this
in the beginning that I

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:40.180
don't want to talk too much
about the obvious stuff.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.850
So let's cover that quickly first, right?

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.080
So what I mean what is the obvious stuff

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.570
about the whole travel discussion?

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:49.680
Of course you will be away
from home Monday to Thursday.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:51.840
Again, I will link another video up here

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.050
where I talked about the typical work week

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.320
in the life of a consultant
if this interests you.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.380
How, like, the schedule
looks like where you are

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.800
at what point in time,
at least, especially like

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.280
until end of 2019 before the
current health situation.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.170
Of course, most people are at home office

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:08.320
but how this plays out,
have a look at that video.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.160
But what I really mean
with the travel is that

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.657
it's really more than that, right?

00:10:12.657 --> 00:10:14.470
And of course the one part of it is that

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:17.780
it can be very glamorous and, you know

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:21.950
you might fly business
class around the country

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.740
a lot of course that feels glamorous.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.470
You have all the status cards of all the

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.490
airlines, of all the big hotel chains.

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:30.643
You might stay in some great,
very, very amazing hotels.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:34.360
These are the nice aspects.
And yes, this is nice,

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.420
and even after several years,
I still enjoyed that, okay?

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:38.730
I mean, with the downside of course

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.590
that you are away from
home, away from the family.

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:42.370
This is still the nice aspect.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.270
But still the reality is
that not every project

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.560
is in a nice big city where you have

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.450
this infrastructure where
you can enjoy all this.

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:53.300
And for me, probably
at least every third or

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:58.070
every fourth project
for me was at some place

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.600
very deep, like in the middle of nowhere

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:04.930
in the countryside where it
was really difficult to get to.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.520
I mean, I will remember being like at some

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.270
very very rural location in the UK.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.750
there was only a discount
carrier taking you there.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.210
So for sure, nothing like business class

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:19.700
or any like great status with lounges

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.760
or so experienced at the airport.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.410
Then there was a long
ride with the, with a car.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.720
Then we need to get that location

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.930
on the logistics would
take you hours every day,

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:31.370
would mean that you would need to wake up

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:33.090
I believe I was waking up at 4:00 AM

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.870
every Monday just to get there.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:38.610
And it was like super late when
I arrived back on Thursday.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:40.420
But then also these places often

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.870
there aren't great hotels
or anything like that.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:46.050
So especially at this
point, I was in a hotel.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.240
It was like really not a great hotel.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.380
And I'm, I'm not like, it's not even that,

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:53.040
you know, I'm the guy who
to whom it is so important,

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.270
that it's so luxurious or whatever

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.940
but it was really not a great place.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.400
It was in the winter, it was cold

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.700
I remember freezing at night because

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:04.000
the heating in this hotel
wasn't working properly.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.790
I just needed to like
take several sweatshirts

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.860
on just because I was literally
freezing there, right?

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:12.620
The food was super bad, there was not

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.660
any restaurant close by that had

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.220
well, like a decent food quality.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.430
And of course, this is so demoralizing.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:20.707
If, you know, you work so much,

00:12:20.707 --> 00:12:23.970
you work so late and you
are in the hotel room

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.670
and then it's cold and the food is bad.

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:29.120
And I mean, this just adds so much

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:32.340
to this also really mental
pressure that you have.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.620
And again, there are some glamorous parts.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.820
Sometimes it can be great.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.400
Again, I had great
experiences in amazing hotels.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.400
Of course, these are the nice sites

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.790
but don't underestimate
how many also very big

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.980
very large companies have sometimes

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:49.980
their headquarters at
very, very rural places.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.700
Or of course, you are not
always at the headquarters.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.430
Maybe you are working
in, in, in production.

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:56.450
And then you are in
some production factory

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.060
somewhere in the middle of nowhere

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.980
working with these people, um,

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.730
it can be tough. And this again, adds

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.200
to this mental situation, to the pressure.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.460
It adds to this overall sometimes really

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:11.230
really bad situation that you
can then find yourself in.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.890
This is just also part of the reality.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.723
This was the second point I
wanted to share here today.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:26.510
The third point is the learning curve.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.020
And specifically what's maybe

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.900
not so great about the learning curve.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:34.070
Because most people want
to join consulting, who

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.160
are interested in a career
in consulting do this

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.670
because they believe that the
learning curve is amazing.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.140
And again, like, overall, I agree.

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:45.150
Overall I believe the
learning curve is great

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:47.180
is amazing, at least much better

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.560
than most other career
paths that you can take.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:52.370
Because specifically
you just have exposure

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.980
to a very high number of industries,

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.850
a very high number of different functions.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.860
Like probably there's no
other career path where like

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.170
in a couple of years you
will likely have worked

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.290
in retail, in automotive, in pharma,

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.403
in telecommunications, I mean, really

00:14:07.403 --> 00:14:10.420
what you see what you can do is great.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:15.230
Those third, to some extent
it does get repetitive.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.170
This is also part of the truth.

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:19.430
And probably this is even worse in,

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.390
for instance, IT consulting types of firms

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.660
where the projects are even longer

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:26.510
the type of projects that
you do are even more similar.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.230
But I would argue even
in strategy consulting

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:32.620
MBB type of consulting
firms, it gets repetitive.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:36.730
Not necessarily regarding
the contents that you do

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.120
because often yes, it is different.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.780
But even here over time you will

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:41.950
be asked to specialize more and more,

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.580
After two or three years,
you will really focus

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:46.500
much more on specific industries,

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.320
specific types of functions,
of types of projects

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.410
because of course is
then valuable knowledge.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.260
And then of course, everybody
wants you to do this again

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.620
because this is the
really something you've

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.770
learned, that you're really good at.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.510
I mean, it makes sense, but of course

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:01.380
then the content start to
repeat after some time.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.640
But even if you do do different things

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.560
the overall structure, the type

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:08.080
of things that you do are very similar.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:10.920
I mean, always like in
the first week, you always

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:15.370
have a client kickoff, to
prepare this client kickoff.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.120
Then you start the project,
you have expert calls,

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.300
calls with internal
experts, other partners

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:22.570
who did similar things
already in the past,

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:25.910
maybe some external aspects,
experts that you talk to.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:27.070
This is then this next phase.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.550
Then you have your
weekly, your fix meetings,

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:31.810
your weekly regular
meetings with the clients

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:33.800
where then you always prepare
the thorough fix document.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.840
You talk about this with the client

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:38.250
then you prepare your
analysis, get some data

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.850
build an Excel model, crunch the numbers

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.280
derive this, share this
back with the client,

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.590
discuss it, then every second week

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.090
you have a steerco.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.330
So it's a big steering committee

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.530
the big committee where usually

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.060
with board level type of members,

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:52.060
you discuss then the results.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:53.680
Again, the process is always the same.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.870
The partner comes in,
discuss this with you.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.380
Then you do an iteration
loop, another iteration loop

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:00.370
until you have the
document then present it

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.693
in front of the board, get the feedback.

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:06.100
So this kind of type of
activities that you do.

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:09.050
These types of discussions.
It really starts to get

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:11.970
repetitive after some point, again,

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:15.120
probably much more interesting
than many other career jobs

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.810
but after you did this a couple of years

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:20.840
it doesn't necessarily
feel like this anymore

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:21.800
like the very first time, like

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:22.747
the very first years you do this.

00:16:22.747 --> 00:16:24.500
And of course, this is
also part of the reason,

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.120
why then after a couple of years,

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.820
many people do switch, right?

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:29.400
Many people do then transition.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:30.930
And of course then once
you're project lead

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:32.410
the new experience that you add is really

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.830
managing the team, leading the team.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:35.230
This is a new experience.

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:37.160
Once you are then a partner,
here the new experience

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.080
is really, are you responsible

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:41.290
for acquiring new business, doing sales,

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:42.730
If you want to call it this way

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.590
of course this is a new experience.

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:47.230
But I would argue
depending on what exactly

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.570
that you do, but then there are

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.160
some exit paths that you
could take that really

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.410
then increase your
learning curve much more.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.170
And here one of the things I missed most

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:58.540
in terms of consulting
in terms of the learning

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.060
for sure was really this
operational experience

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.670
because let's be frank,
it's very different

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:06.080
to just be the expert
just tell other people

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.810
in a smart way, what they should do.

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.600
You know, this one thing, and of course,

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.370
this is important and
a great skill to have

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.150
you understand
intellectually what's right,

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:17.820
but then really implementing
something like this

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:20.660
in an organization, talking to the people,

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:24.240
making them do the things
that you want them to do.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:27.140
All of this might sound
obvious to you as a consultant.

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:29.810
And probably I even thought
that this was rather easy,

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:30.840
you know, when I was a consultant.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:32.690
But now after a couple of years and more

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.130
operational roads after I have consulting.

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.660
So you want to divert for two years at a

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.130
at a CTO position in a retail company.

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.930
Now, since this year transitioned

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.620
into a chief revenue officer position

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.440
at a medium sized company here in Munich.

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.880
When you're responsible for your team

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:50.840
and you need to talk and
work with real people.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.360
And maybe then also with people where not

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:55.170
everybody has an Ivy
league education where not

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:58.380
everybody is getting
paid a six digit salary

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.910
because of course these people
are then super motivated,

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:03.200
will do everything you
ask them to do, right?

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.470
But maybe with people
also with other profiles

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:08.360
motivating these people, influencing them

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:09.540
to really work together with you

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.950
on the things that are important to you.

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:12.310
And then also that they do it the way

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.760
that you believe is right,
and you know is right.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.750
This is really a significant challenge.

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.810
And I really think that
this is an experience

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:20.140
that you do not learn, do not get

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.240
in consulting because there,
for you often just stops

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:27.480
in the theory and is for
most types of projects.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.720
So this is my third
point. Let me just recap,

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:31.790
First, the pressure that you are on,

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:35.730
early on can be immense,
can be unbearable.

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:38.090
At least it feels at
times that it's unbearable

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.660
and can really crush you, especially

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:42.140
if you are, like your mental health

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.970
isn't already in a strong
place at the beginning.

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:44.940
You're not really able to build

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.660
some good resilience strategies here.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.020
Second, this travel that just adds

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:52.630
on it can be really, really tough for you.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.310
And third, the sort of repetition.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.420
Yes, the learning curve
is great, but maybe

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:59.287
not always as great as
you think it is, or,

00:18:59.287 --> 00:19:02.283
as you think it will be
when you join consulting.

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:05.860
These are my truths. These are the things

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:08.330
where I believe that
maybe consulting is not

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.770
the right career path for everybody.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:11.400
And at least I believe it's very fair

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:13.150
that you know about this before

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:14.950
you start your career in consulting.

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:18.870
This is just my perspective, my opinion,

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.140
of course, I trust other people

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.980
might've had different experiences also.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.480
So I'm not claiming that this is now

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.800
the reality, the truth for everybody.

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:27.540
I love to get your
perspective on that as well.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.240
I mean, what were these
maybe darker moments

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:33.520
darker situations, not so
great experiences that you had.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.600
Let me know in the comments I'd love to,

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:37.010
to, to interact with you on that.

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:38.820
As you know, I will do my
best to answer every comment

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.150
but I trust it would also be interesting

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.330
to other people watching
this video to learn

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:44.600
from your other experiences as well.

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.320
And, you know it, as always
if you took some value

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:48.750
out of this video, I'd really love you

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.460
If you hit the like button and

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.730
subscribe for more content like this.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.340
Also big thank you to all the members

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.610
of Firm Learning for your support.

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:56.950
I really appreciate it.

